    "review_findings": [
      "The launch script replaced a killed headless browser exit status with zero. That reported exit code does not establish a clean browser exit.",
      "The headless test used the user-agent substring position, not the documented addition 30 + 41.",
      "The top-level Windows verification date predates the supplied Chromium screenshot. No original Chromium serial log is present in this worktree.",
      "A browser title, rendered pixels and TCP connect attempts alone do not prove successful certificate validation."
    ]
  },
  "review_2026_10_17": {
    "date": "2026-10-17",
    "status": "completed_with_limitations",
    "chromium_rebuilt": false,
    "build_log": "runtime/review/build.log",
    "notes": [
      "Headless success requires computed DOM, raw exit status zero, and timeout flag zero. Killed or timed-out processes cannot be substituted for successful runs.",
      "musl i386 thread stack fields at words 13/14 are updated without overwriting allocation ownership at words 11/12. Thread slots are claimed atomically; native stacks are reused only after NT termination. Unmapped TLS and child-TID pointers are cleared.",
      "Adapter and driver failures propagate instead of supplying guessed hardware identity. Fixed QEMU network configuration is reported as read-only. DNS/ICMP replies are validated; netd records actual established TCP connections and received payload.",
      "Registry enumeration creates and verifies its own volatile value instead of passing when an optional setup key is absent.",
      "The GUI probe requires mapped XFCE components, a Yahoo browser title, and varied pixels in multiple webpage rows. These observations do not establish TLS security or identify the renderer.",
      "The 14 host tests include explicit NT/X11 mocks and a 16000-lifecycle thread-slot stress test; they are not guest runtime evidence. Guest test results are recorded separately.",
      "Superseded by the 2026-10-18 current_review. docs/screenshots/verified-xfce.png and verified-chromium.png were replaced on 2026-10-18; the hashes in this record identify the earlier captures (verified-minimal.png is unchanged)."
    ],
