    "input_checks": {
      "method": "QMP send-key and input-send-event (relative motion, buttons, wheel) into the emulated PS/2 keyboard and IntelliMouse; the same QEMU input path the SDL window uses",
      "ps2_mouse_packet_size": 4,
      "minimal_shell": {
        "commands": [
          "expr 137 - 29",
          "echo hello | grep h; echo x | head -1; echo rc=$?",
          "grep -c root /etc/passwd; ls /WINDOWS/system32 | grep -i -e ntoskrnl -e hal",
          "ls /WINDOWS/system32/drivers | grep -c sys; busybox --list | wc -l",
          "lsmod -a | grep -i -e ntoskrnl -e hal -e rtl"
        ],
        "observed": [
          "108",
          "hello, x, rc=0",
          "1; hal.dll, ntoskrnl.exe",
          "22; 276",
          "ntoskrnl.exe, hal.dll and rtl8139.sys loaded"
        ]
      },
      "xfce": [
        "Mouse motion and a left click focused the terminal; typed commands executed (captures below)"
      ],
      "chromium": [
        "Wheel down 4 clicks scrolled yahoo.com to later stories; wheel up 4 clicks returned to the top",
        "Left click on the Yahoo search field opened its search overlay; typed \"NT kernel\" appeared",
        "Clicking the XFCE taskbar Terminal button raised the terminal over Chromium"
      ]
    },
    "fixes": [
      "PS/2 driver (rootfs, chromium_rootfs): enables the IntelliMouse wheel (200/100/80 sample-rate sequence, ID 3) and parses 4-byte packets; the wheel delta is carried in Buttons bits 8-15.",
      "X11 framebuffer bridge: wheel deltas become XTEST button 4/5 clicks; only bits 0-2 are compared as button state.",
      "Chromium RAM disk enlarged to 192 MiB: with 128 MiB the GUI profile could not create its ProcessSingleton socket directory and Chromium aborted after the headless check.",
      "In-process vfork (all shims): each exited child is recorded for wait4, so pipelines no longer reuse one PID and report status 255.",
      "In-process applet exec (all shims): musl stdio state, bb_common_bufsiz1 and xfunc_error_retval are reset as after a real exec, and restored for the parent. grep previously reused stale patterns and head/grep saw a stale stdin EOF.",
      "Minimal shim: vfork snapshots the whole descriptor table with per-child handle and pipe-end references (refcounted pipes, 4 MiB on-demand buffers), fixing \"can't duplicate file descriptor\" and Broken pipe in every pipeline.",
      "TCGETS returns ENOTTY for pipes, sockets, /dev/null and files, including redirected stdin/stdout/stderr, so ls no longer emits terminal columns and colors into pipes.",
      "mremap copies data whenever the new mapping succeeds, not only when the address is below 2 GiB.",
      "mmap failure in the Chromium shim prints a one-time NT address-space summary (free, largest free block, commit/reserve) for diagnosis."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "A 2 GiB user address space bounds single-process Chromium. An earlier long session hit STATUS_NO_MEMORY on 3.4 MiB reservations; the final runs, including repeated scrolling, had no mapping failures. /3GB boot was tried and faults in NTLDR during the kernel hand-off, so it is not used.",
      "Chromium GUI uses CPU rendering; repaint after scrolling or typing takes several seconds.",
      "Chromium browser assets still require IDE attachment; USB browser verification is unsupported.",
      "Input checks used QMP injection rather than a person at the SDL window; both feed QEMU's emulated PS/2 devices."
    ],
